from pathlib import Path
import json,re,html
O=Path('outputs');d=json.loads((O/'phate-check-diagnostics.json').read_text());points=json.loads((O/'phate-check-points.json').read_text())
scripts=re.findall(r'<script[^>]*>(.*?)</script>',(O/'atlas-alignment-report.html').read_text(),flags=re.S);lib=max(scripts,key=len);assert len(lib)>1000000
names={'alignment':'Alignment distances · baseline','composition_pca50':'Composition features · PCA 50','composition_no_pca':'Composition features · no PCA','profile_pca50':'Alignment-distance profiles · PCA 50'}
rows=''.join('<tr><td>'+v+'</td><td>'+names[m]+'</td><td>'+str(r['t'])+'</td><td>'+f"{r['mean_alignment_neighbor_recall15']:.1%}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r['mean_own_input_neighbor_recall15']:.1%}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r.get('mean_original_feature_neighbor_recall15',0):.1%}"+'</td><td>'+str(r['graph_components'])+'</td></tr>' for v,s in d['views'].items() for m,r in s['fits'].items())
validrows=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(g)+'</td><td>'+str(r['n'])+'</td><td>'+f"{r['median_identity']:.1%}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r['median_min_coverage']:.1%}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r['median_distance']:.3f}"+'</td></tr>' for g,r in d['validation_by_group'].items())
corrows=''.join('<tr><td>'+v+'</td><td>'+f"{r['distance_spearman_log_length_ratio']:.3f}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r['distance_spearman_chain_count_difference']:.3f}"+'</td><td>'+f"{r['random_pair_distance']['median']:.3f}"+'</td></tr>' for v,r in d['views'].items())
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>PHATE checks and PCA comparison</title><style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui;color:#203047;background:#f6f8fb;margin:0}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:24px}section{background:white;border:1px solid #dde4ed;border-radius:12px;padding:22px;margin:22px 0}h1{font-size:30px}h2{font-size:23px}.controls{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap}.controls label{font-size:14px;font-weight:650;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px}select{padding:9px;font:inherit;background:white;border:1px solid #bdc9d7;border-radius:6px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.card{border:1px solid #dae2ed;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;min-width:0}.card h3{margin:0}.map{height:400px}.muted{color:#58697c;font-size:14px}.note{padding:12px;border-left:4px solid #d99a25;background:#fffaf0}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid #dce4ec;text-align:left}.table{overflow:auto}a{color:#225b9d}@media(max-width:850px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style><main><h1>PHATE diagnostics and PCA comparison</h1><p>The existing alignment map is the baseline. These checks reuse the same plotted cohort and frozen split. No sequence selection or train/validation membership was changed.</p><section><h2>What the checks found</h2><p>The alignment distance distribution is narrow near its upper limit: median random-pair distance is 0.979 for whole complexes and 0.949 for interfaces. Its affinity kernel is broad, with median effective neighbourhood sizes of 5,783 and 1,884 respectively. This explains why k=15 still produces rapid smoothing and a compressed interface cloud.</p><p>PCA 50 makes the original composition-feature maps substantially less dominated by outliers. It is a useful overview, with a trade-off in local detail; compare the common-reference neighbourhood metrics below. The PCA-on-distance-profiles experiment has disconnected groups and a very strong interface-size association (absolute axis correlation 0.97), so it is retained as an exploratory comparison.</p><p>The report opens with composition features + PCA 50. The alignment baseline remains selectable and unchanged. <a href="phate-check-pca50-overview.pdf">PCA overview PDF</a> · <a href="phate-check-pca50-overview.png">PCA overview PNG</a></p></section><section id="comparison"><h2>Controlled comparisons</h2><div class="controls">
<label>Features<select id="view"><option value="whole">Whole sequences</option><option value="interface">Interface residues</option></select></label>
<label>Representation<select id="method"><option value="alignment">Alignment distances · baseline</option><option value="composition_pca50" selected>Composition features · PCA 50</option><option value="composition_no_pca">Composition features · no PCA</option><option value="profile_pca50">Alignment-distance profiles · PCA 50</option></select></label>
<label>Plot extent<select id="extent"><option value="full">All points</option><option value="focus">1–99% per-axis zoom</option></select></label>
<label>Highlight<select id="split"><option value="all">All splits</option><option value="val">Validation</option><option value="train">Training</option><option value="test">Test</option></select></label>
<label>Chain count<select id="chains"><option value="all">All</option><option value="1">Monomers</option><option value="2">Two chains</option><option value="3">Three or more</option></select></label>
<label>Colour<select id="colour"><option value="dataset">Dataset</option><option value="chain_count">Chain count</option><option value="length">Sequence / interface size</option></select></label></div>
<p id="fitstats" class="muted"></p><p id="fit-warning" class="note" hidden></p><p class="muted">Circles: training · Diamonds: validation · Crosses: test. Grey points retain the full reference population. The zoom changes only the displayed axes; it does not remove points or refit PHATE. Axes are shared initially across dataset panels; each representation is independently embedded.</p><div class="grid">CARDS</div></section>
<section><h2>PCA and neighbourhood preservation</h2><p><strong>The controlled PCA test is composition PCA 50 versus composition without PCA.</strong> Both use the original 840-dimensional features and cosine distance; other PHATE settings are held fixed. The alignment baseline supplies precomputed distances, for which PHATE disables its feature PCA. Applying PCA to rows of an alignment-distance matrix instead treats each row as a distance-profile feature vector; that separate comparison uses 50 PCs and Euclidean distance. It changes the representation and is not a direct PCA-on/off test of alignment geometry.</p><p>All fits use k=15, decay=40, 500 landmarks, automatic diffusion time, gamma=1, metric MDS with SMACOF, and seed 20261011. Verified identical alignment-distance profiles are fitted once and all entries mapped back. The baseline coordinates are checked against the saved map.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>View</th><th>Representation</th><th>Auto t</th><th>Alignment-neighbour recall@15</th><th>Own-input neighbour recall@15</th><th>Original-feature recall@15 (common reference)</th><th>Graph components</th></tr>FITROWS</table></div><p class="muted">Recall is the fraction of the 15 high-dimensional nearest neighbours retained among the 15 nearest neighbours in 2D, evaluated on a fixed random sample of up to 1,024 unique profiles. Approximate ties are not specially weighted. Own-input recall uses each representation after its PCA step, when applicable; values across different representations measure different geometries. Original-feature recall uses the same unreduced 840-dimensional features and cosine distance for every map, allowing the PCA/no-PCA comparison to share a reference. These are local-detail checks, not biological validation or a complete PHATE quality score.</p></section>
<section><h2>Are length and chain count influencing the distances?</h2><div class="table"><table><tr><th>View</th><th>Distance vs absolute log length ratio (Spearman)</th><th>Distance vs chain-count difference (Spearman)</th><th>Median random-pair distance</th></tr>CORROWS</table></div><p class="muted">Based on up to 100,000 random pairs of unique profiles. Correlation is descriptive, not evidence that a covariate alone causes the layout. Use the chain-count filter and colour selector to inspect the effect.</p></section>
<section><h2>Are the nearest matches meaningful?</h2><p>Local BLOSUM62 alignments were independently traced for nearest neighbours in another dataset and nearest entries in the <strong>plotted training sample</strong>. Up to 80 query profiles per dataset/split were selected deterministically. The table below includes validation queries only. It is not an exhaustive nearest-training search and does not replace the original leakage audit.</p><div class="table"><table><tr><th>View / validation group</th><th>Queries</th><th>Median identity</th><th>Median minimum coverage</th><th>Median distance</th></tr>VALIDROWS</table></div><p>Identity = identical residues / alignment columns, including gap columns. Coverage counts residues within each matched local alignment; unmatched chains contribute zero covered residues. Minimum coverage is the lesser of whole-query and whole-target coverage. Interface values describe ordered contact subsequences, with non-contact positions omitted.</p><img src="phate-check-nearest-training.png" style="width:100%;height:auto" alt="Validation nearest-training identity, coverage and distance distributions"><p><a href="phate-check-nearest-matches.csv">Nearest-match table (CSV)</a> · <a href="phate-check-nearest-matches.json">Chain-level alignments summary</a> · <a href="phate-check-nearest-training.pdf">Audit figure PDF</a> · <a href="phate-check-diagnostics.json">Full diagnostics</a> · <a href="atlas-alignment-report.html">Baseline report</a></p></section><p><a href="https://phate.readthedocs.io/en/stable/_modules/phate/phate.html">PHATE implementation and parameter documentation</a></p></main><script>LIBRARY</script><script>
(()=>{const points=POINTS, diagnostics=DIAGNOSTICS;const datasets=['ATLAS','PINDER','pKPDB','Benchmark'],colors=['#0072B2','#009E73','#D55E00','#882E72'];const val=id=>document.getElementById(id).value;
function render(){const view=val('view'),method=val('method'),key=view+'-'+method,all=points.filter(p=>p[key]);const xs=all.map(p=>p[key][0]).sort((a,b)=>a-b),ys=all.map(p=>p[key][1]).sort((a,b)=>a-b);const q=(x,f)=>x[Math.floor((x.length-1)*f)];const focus=val('extent')==='focus';let x0=q(xs,focus?.01:0),x1=q(xs,focus?.99:1),y0=q(ys,focus?.01:0),y1=q(ys,focus?.99:1);let px=(x1-x0)*.06,py=(y1-y0)*.06;x0-=px;x1+=px;y0-=py;y1+=py;const f=diagnostics.views[view].fits[method];document.getElementById('fitstats').textContent='Auto t = '+f.t+' · Alignment-neighbour recall@15: '+(100*f.mean_alignment_neighbor_recall15).toFixed(1)+'% · Own-input recall@15: '+(100*f.mean_own_input_neighbor_recall15).toFixed(1)+'% · Graph components: '+f.graph_components+(val('colour')==='chain_count'?' · Colour: blue = 1 chain, orange = 2, purple = 3+':'');
const warnings=[];if(f.graph_components>1)warnings.push('Exploratory: the graph has '+f.graph_components+' disconnected components. Distances between separated groups are not reliable.');const rho=Math.max(...f.axis_length_spearman.filter(x=>x!==null).map(Math.abs));if(rho>.8)warnings.push('Strong size association: maximum absolute axis–length Spearman correlation = '+rho.toFixed(2)+'.');if(method==='alignment')warnings.push('Broad affinity weights: median effective neighbourhood size = '+Math.round(f.effective_neighbors.median).toLocaleString()+'. k=15 sets an adaptive bandwidth, not a hard limit of 15 graph neighbours.');const warning=document.getElementById('fit-warning');warning.hidden=!warnings.length;warning.textContent=warnings.join(' ');
datasets.forEach((ds,i)=>{const selected=all.filter(p=>p.dataset===ds&&(val('split')==='all'||p.split===val('split'))&&(val('chains')==='all'||(val('chains')==='3'?p.chains>=3:p.chains===Number(val('chains')))));const outside=selected.filter(p=>p[key][0]<x0||p[key][0]>x1||p[key][1]<y0||p[key][1]>y1).length;document.getElementById('count-'+i).textContent=selected.length.toLocaleString()+' highlighted'+(focus?' · '+outside+' outside zoom':'');const traces=[{type:'scattergl',mode:'markers',x:all.map(p=>p[key][0]),y:all.map(p=>p[key][1]),marker:{size:3,color:'#a6b0bd',opacity:.12},hoverinfo:'skip',showlegend:false}];for(const [sp,symbol] of [['train','circle'],['val','diamond'],['test','x']]){const pp=selected.filter(p=>p.split===sp);if(!pp.length)continue;let color=colors[i];if(val('colour')==='chain_count')color=pp.map(p=>p.chains===1?'#0072B2':p.chains===2?'#D55E00':'#882E72');if(val('colour')==='length')color=pp.map(p=>Math.log10(view==='whole'?p.residues:Math.max(p.interface_residues,1)));const marker={size:sp==='train'?5:7,symbol,color,opacity:.7};if(val('colour')==='length'){Object.assign(marker,{colorscale:'Viridis',cmin:0,cmax:4,showscale:sp===pp[0].split,colorbar:{title:'log10 size',thickness:10}});marker.showscale=traces.length===1;}traces.push({type:'scattergl',mode:'markers',x:pp.map(p=>p[key][0]),y:pp.map(p=>p[key][1]),text:pp.map(p=>p.id+' · '+p.group+'<br>'+p.chains+' chains · '+p.residues+' residues · '+p.interface_residues+' interface residues'),marker,showlegend:false,hovertemplate:'%{text}<extra></extra>'});}Plotly.react('map-'+i,traces,{template:'plotly_white',margin:{l:50,r:val('colour')==='length'?70:15,t:10,b:45},xaxis:{title:'PHATE 1',range:[x0,x1],zeroline:false},yaxis:{title:'PHATE 2',range:[y0,y1],zeroline:false}},{responsive:true,displaylogo:false});});}
for(const id of ['view','method','extent','split','chains','colour'])document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('change',render);render();})();
</script></html>'''
cards=''.join(f'<div class="card"><h3 style="color:{c}">{ds}</h3><p class="muted" id="count-{i}"></p><div class="map" id="map-{i}"></div></div>' for i,(ds,c) in enumerate(zip(['ATLAS','PINDER','pKPDB','Benchmark'],['#0072B2','#009E73','#D55E00','#882E72'])))
for key,value in [('CARDS',cards),('FITROWS',rows),('CORROWS',corrows),('VALIDROWS',validrows),('POINTS',json.dumps(points,separators=(',',':'))),('DIAGNOSTICS',json.dumps(d,separators=(',',':'))),('LIBRARY',lib)]:page=page.replace(key,value)
(O/'phate-check-report.html').write_text(page);print('Wrote',O/'phate-check-report.html')
